{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1385760-storypath-star-wars","id":1385760,"title":"Storypath Star Wars","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-05T00:10:28-07:00","id":1385760,"title":"Storypath Star Wars","content":"So I watched ( finally ) Episode 9 of <b>Star Wars</b> Saga. ( Yupi! ) And thought that some SW RPG could be good. In years I wanted to run - when having good plot in mind - SW game based on <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> rules engine. But the<b> Storypath</b> is more epic 'sister' to it, seems to work more with the SW feel. As <b>Trinity</b> is S-F rules setting, it feel it's forum to me more appropriate as place for the possible fan conversions.<br /> <br /> Some questions that should shape SW iteration of game engine:<br /> 1. <b>Momentum</b> <b>-&gt; Force Points</b> - Of course, I would make it into Force Points, like it was in the even <b>Saga Edition</b> ( D20 SW ). Question is - <b>How to reflect Dark Side Points? </b>You can just take them as free Momentum, but they stay on the character, tainting it?<br /> 2. <b><a href=\"https://starwars.fandom.com/wiki/Species/Legends\" target=\"_blank\">Species</a></b> - I can see both arguments for and against making your Species to giving you extra dots in Attributes. Maybe middle ground would be simple +1 dots in one Attribute only? Still most of Galaxy is human and probably get's free Edge, then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-05-2020, 03:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T01:06:12-07:00","id":1385771,"title":"","content":"1a. Your approach is ok if you go for a team of non-active force users, basically non-Jedi. Once you add a Jedi, Momentum will be drained by him (because he have special uses for it) very often, leaving the others with no options. If you give active force users another pool, like Inspiration or Psi, the game would flow better (as I see), and Momentum would be a perfect Force Point. Must remember that Momentum is a collective pool, so characters that are dependent on the pool can\u2019t work fine together.<br /> 1b. Dark Side being an extra Dice you gain when spending Momentum is great. But staking uses is complex because you don\u2019t have a good pool for that, 5 is kind of too low for a long term stacking. Using a Quantum Flux/Transcendence analogue is an option, it may grant extra dice when using dark side on higher T, but require you to resist for using it every time you spend a momentum. Balancing the effort to let the flux/Transcendence fo would be a great effort, I mean, it\u2019s easy to go straight dark or keep it on the light (in game terms), but playing a grey Jedi must be possible.<br /> <br /> 2. Two options, different templates for different species or a \u201cspecies Edge\u201d for every species (including human).<br /> The first option gives us more work to creat a new species, and maybe give some really different species, but in the end, Star Wars species are all pretty human, and I don\u2019t mean a guy on costume, I mean, they are all same scale with differences being on the same range as humans, let\u2019s say, a Wookie is strong, but he is not super strong, they are more savages on fight than properly stronger than humans. You can force a certain Arena or Approach as primary for different species, or give an extra point In an attribute or skill, but it\u2019s more limiting than interesting in my mind.<br /> I would go for one or more Species Edges that can be bought ONLY by member of certain species, let\u2019s say, Wookiee have a Savage Fighter that grant an enhancement on close combat and Stronger than Many that allow them to buy a 6th dot in Might. Humans have an Edge for Strong in the Force that make them better in using Momentum or give them a higher limit on the number of skill tricks, I don\u2019t know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 05-05-2020, 04:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T01:24:40-07:00","id":1385774,"title":"","content":"Quick ideas, since I'm stuck at work.<br /> <br /> I'm a fan of making it player-driven, as in you don't get points for simply doing things, you make an active choice to go dark. And that should be tempting. <br /> <br /> You could take the Corruption rules and modify them for to have a Light Side Pool (Momentum) and Dark Side Pool (Corruption). Normal characters can tap into the dark side and instead of spending Momentum they add dice to the Dark Side Pool that the Storyguide gets to use later. <br /> <br /> For Force-users I would make the Dark Side feel stronger, or rather faster. Use the Dark Side and get 2 additional successes (not Enhancement, straight successes). In combat, use it to get a free damage or critical. <br /> The cost: take a Dark Side Condition, I would put 4 levels. Fear -&gt; Anger -&gt; Hate -&gt; Lost to the Dark Side. <br /> <br /> The conditions would give Enhancements and Drawbacks, the first three have a Resolution that the characters can take to redeem themselves. The last condition could mean that the character becomes a npc, but only another character can resolve the condition. <br /> <br /> For species. Keeping it simple, give out 4 extra dots of Edges, they can ignore Path requirements if the Edge fits the Species?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5961-lazygm","name":"LazyGM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T01:30:17-07:00","id":1385775,"title":"","content":"LazyGM, Great ideas for Dark Side! Better than the Trancendence approach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T01:33:38-07:00","id":1385776,"title":"","content":"Mateus Luz, thank you, I didn't see your post before posting mine, apologies if I seemed rude by ignoring you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5961-lazygm","name":"LazyGM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T02:20:07-07:00","id":1385784,"title":"","content":"Quick answer to Species - <b>Giving Wookies Scale +1 on Might base feats sounds to me okay</b>. Making it the Edge or 'in-build' Specie's trait works fine for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T16:48:37-07:00","id":1390096,"title":"","content":"It would be interesting t ok have force points sumiliar to Psi Points representing your total.<br /> <br /> One side was light and the other side was dark and your balance point slides left or right light or dark.<br /> <br /> Didn't Aberrant have something like this","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T16:49:40-07:00","id":1390097,"title":"","content":"Oh and let's say you have 10 points 7 light and three dark using the 8th point may cause the dark side to grow","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T17:38:16-07:00","id":1390121,"title":"","content":"I like your idea. You could go on a similar way to Virtues from Scion, Light in one side Dark in the other, using Light often make you virtuous in the light and vice versa.<br /> <br /> If you think like that, you are powerful to light side powers and weak on dark side powers when Virtuous in the light, and the reverse when in the dark side. You move to the dark side when you follow your emotions and to the light side when you don\u2019t.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T22:19:18-07:00","id":1390197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1385760-storypath-star-wars?p=1390121#post1390121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like your idea. You could go on a similar way to Virtues from Scion, Light in one side Dark in the other, using Light often make you virtuous in the light and vice versa.<br /> <br /> If you think like that, you are powerful to light side powers and weak on dark side powers when Virtuous in the light, and the reverse when in the dark side. You move to the dark side when you follow your emotions and to the light side when you don\u2019t.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hell ya, I still think there was something from 1st edition Aeon or Aberrant maybe Taint level, I need to grab my 1e books and do some checking, and look at Virtues from Scion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T17:14:49-07:00","id":1392077,"title":"","content":"It isn't perfect, and it just off the cuff, but maybe piggyback on the Dysfunctin mechanic, and certain Modes are more Dark than Light, so when you go into Dysfunction how it manifests takes some queues off the Mode being considered Light or Dark.<br /> <br /> This runs into one of my personal pet peeves, the exulting of &quot;Grey Jedi&quot; as the Answer, but it's a start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T17:53:59-07:00","id":1392083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1385760-storypath-star-wars?p=1392077#post1392077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It isn't perfect, and it just off the cuff, but maybe piggyback on the Dysfunctin mechanic, and certain Modes are more Dark than Light, so when you go into Dysfunction how it manifests takes some queues off the Mode being considered Light or Dark.<br /> <br /> This runs into one of my personal pet peeves, the exulting of &quot;Grey Jedi&quot; as the Answer, but it's a start.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your idea is interesting, but Dysfunction is more permanent than my understanding of temptation from the dark side.<br /> <br /> Yet, it can be part of the system, let\u2019s say, being trained as a Jedi (light side), makes you better in Light side powers and makes it easier to remain in the light side of the balance, same for the dark side, and a Gray Jedi would be the one that can keep balance both in skill and behavior.<br /> <br /> Why I think that, it\u2019s all about Luke in the Emperor Throne Room in Death Star. The emperor can feel the dark side inside Luke and start using this in his favor (he has a power for that, it\u2019s not an standard dark side effect), yet Luke is trained exclusively in the light side skills (trained only by Jedi), and so would not be able to be tempted as it would make him go against his dysfunction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T06:45:15-07:00","id":1393770,"title":"","content":"Personally for using The Force I\u2019d lean far away from Aberrant stuff and Psion stuff. I\u2019d go with something more like the Talent facets and then use gifts for things that go beyond letting The Force flow through you to enhance some action like piloting a pod racer or firing a proton torpedo into a vent. I think things like Force lightning or the stuff that looks like D&amp;D magic spells is better off treated as edge cases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T19:39:12-07:00","id":1394217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1385760-storypath-star-wars?p=1392083#post1392083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your idea is interesting, but Dysfunction is more permanent than my understanding of temptation from the dark side.<br /> <br /> Yet, it can be part of the system, let\u2019s say, being trained as a Jedi (light side), makes you better in Light side powers and makes it easier to remain in the light side of the balance, same for the dark side, and a Gray Jedi would be the one that can keep balance both in skill and behavior.<br /> <br /> Why I think that, it\u2019s all about Luke in the Emperor Throne Room in Death Star. The emperor can feel the dark side inside Luke and start using this in his favor (he has a power for that, it\u2019s not an standard dark side effect), yet Luke is trained exclusively in the light side skills (trained only by Jedi), and so would not be able to be tempted as it would make him go against his dysfunction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dysfunction goes away once you bring your mode dots back into allignment, but also has the benefit of boosting the power out of allignment, so seems to go right along. The deeper down you go, the more powerful you are, and the harder it is to come back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-10T06:58:11-07:00","id":1478490,"title":"","content":"Playing now <b>LEGO SW Skywalker Saga</b> - and reading more <b>Trinity 2E </b>cores - I think best would be make <b>'Society = Species / Culture</b>' Path, like in basic <b>TC</b>. Most would be <b>Species</b>, but somehow you would get character raised in <b>Culture</b> - like Mandalorian or Jedi Order, for example.<br /> <br /> <b>Force-Sensitivity</b> ( <b>FS</b> for short ) would then be, probably, be an Edge - many characters are <b>Jedi + FS</b>, but others are simply <b>FS</b> - and some are even <b>Jedi &amp; not FS</b> in lore, <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-10-2022, 10:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-10T09:25:42-07:00","id":1478498,"title":"","content":"In TC, as a general rule, species is a Template that you add to the basic character, and you may have an origin path (or many) related to the place the species is common.<br /> <br /> I personally would make Force Sensitivity a Edge that any character (except Droids, apparently) can have, but that is actually very rare. The Force Sensitive Edge would allow the character to learn modes.<br /> <br /> Jedi would need to have the Force Sensitive to become one, but Jedi would be a path, usually a Origin path for the Republic Era Jedi, or a Role path for later members (point to Luke, Grogo, and a few others, but not the Skywalker saga characters).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-10T14:57:12-07:00","id":1478516,"title":"","content":"I believe that, when you use a Force point for Dark Side, it gives you 2 Enhancement but it also gives you a tick in a Dark Side meter. The provides an ongoing Complication in certain circumstances. If not bought off, then it gets higher. When it reaches a certain point, you have a Limit Break similar to Exalted. Mark that Limit Break on a Corruption meter so to speak. When it hits a certain level? Bam. Lost to Dark Side. You can then use Light Side force points or else scenes wherein you are focusing on the Light Side of the Force to bring the Complication down.<br /> <br /> It has a bit more mechanics but it fits, IMO, of tapping into the Dark Side and how, in the long term, it can bring you down. It also reflects how, when you reach certain points, then there is never going to be a chance to become &quot;pure&quot; again....the taint will always be there on you. Also, it shows how you have to work to get rid of the Dark Side but that it IS possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}